cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or adapt the Umuntu Codex, please cite it."
title: "The Umuntu Codex"
abstract: >-
  A conduct codex for autonomous AI coding agents, skinned as the ethics of Ubuntu
  (the Nguni Bantu philosophy, "a person is a person through other persons") — four
  disciplines (the Commons, Indaba, Speaking True, Harambee), each rule carrying an
  observable falsifier. Offered with respect. Part of a small family of conduct harnesses.
type: dataset
